{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>החרה החזיק</b> — From the root of חרון (burning anger). The sense: his anger burned against himself over the delay of the work, and he strengthened his hand for the task a second time." "<b>והחרה</b> — A verb derived from the augmented heavy stem [binyan], and likewise: ויחר עליו אפו (and his anger burned against him)."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:13.108202517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}